1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,410
In fourteen ninety-two, a man stepped off a boat onto a beach.

2
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:08,380
He pushed a flag into the sand.

3
00:00:08,870 --> 00:00:11,180
Then he said the island belonged to Spain.

4
00:00:11,630 --> 00:00:13,450
But people already lived on that island.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,070
They were standing right there, watching him.

6
00:00:16,540 --> 00:00:17,956
Nobody asked them anything.

7
00:00:18,406 --> 00:00:19,984
So why did anyone believe him?

8
00:00:21,284 --> 00:00:22,944
Look closely at the flag he carried.

9
00:00:23,394 --> 00:00:25,184
It was white, with a green cross.

10
00:00:25,634 --> 00:00:28,174
Under the cross were two letters.

11
00:00:28,644 --> 00:00:30,454
F and Y. The F was for Fernando, the king.

12
00:00:30,904 --> 00:00:32,749
The Y was for Ysabel, the queen.

13
00:00:33,199 --> 00:00:39,780
Back then, people spelled Isabella with a Y. Two letters, because Spain had a king and a queen at the same time.

14
00:00:41,080 --> 00:00:42,540
Here is the strange part.

15
00:00:42,990 --> 00:00:45,400
The flag was not meant for the people on the beach.

16
00:00:45,850 --> 00:00:46,700
They could not read it.

17
00:00:47,150 --> 00:00:48,510
It was not in their language.

18
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,190
The flag was a message for other kings, far away in Europe.

19
00:00:52,640 --> 00:00:53,849
And the message was simple.

20
00:00:54,299 --> 00:00:55,333
I got here first.

21
00:00:56,633 --> 00:00:58,423
So the kings made deals with each other.

22
00:00:58,913 --> 00:01:03,683
In fourteen ninety-four, Spain and Portugal drew a line down a map of the ocean.

23
00:01:04,233 --> 00:01:06,653
Everything on this side would belong to Spain.

24
00:01:07,193 --> 00:01:09,573
Everything on that side would belong to Portugal.

25
00:01:10,023 --> 00:01:11,393
They had never seen most of it.

26
00:01:11,843 --> 00:01:13,879
And they never asked the people who lived there.

27
00:01:15,179 --> 00:01:16,709
Portugal did not trust cloth.

28
00:01:17,219 --> 00:01:19,959
Their sailors carried heavy stone posts on their ships.

29
00:01:20,429 --> 00:01:22,879
When they landed, they planted a post in the ground.

30
00:01:23,369 --> 00:01:25,549
A flag rips, and rots, and burns.

31
00:01:26,029 --> 00:01:27,209
A stone just stays.

32
00:01:27,659 --> 00:01:30,184
Some of those stone posts are still standing today.

33
00:01:31,484 --> 00:01:33,534
France used big wooden crosses.

34
00:01:34,004 --> 00:01:40,184
In fifteen thirty-four, a sailor named Cartier put up a cross taller than five grown-ups standing on each other.

35
00:01:40,734 --> 00:01:43,404
A chief named Donnacona told him to take it down.

36
00:01:43,954 --> 00:01:46,514
Cartier said it was only a marker, nothing more.

37
00:01:46,964 --> 00:01:48,942
That was not true, and Cartier knew it.

38
00:01:50,242 --> 00:01:52,722
England showed up almost a hundred years late.

39
00:01:53,252 --> 00:01:57,032
In sixteen oh seven, they carved the king's name into a wooden cross.

40
00:01:57,482 --> 00:01:58,562
Jacobus Rex.

41
00:01:59,012 --> 00:02:00,742
That is Latin for James the King.

42
00:02:01,192 --> 00:02:06,332
It is the same idea as F and Y. But a name on a cross does not feed anybody.

43
00:02:06,812 --> 00:02:08,851
What really kept England there was a plant.

44
00:02:09,302 --> 00:02:10,102
Tobacco.

45
00:02:11,137 --> 00:02:14,337
Here is the last thing, and it is the part worth remembering.

46
00:02:14,837 --> 00:02:17,037
Every one of those places already had a name.

47
00:02:17,517 --> 00:02:19,317
The island was called Guanahani.

48
00:02:19,867 --> 00:02:21,937
The town by the river was Stadacona.

49
00:02:22,457 --> 00:02:24,757
The land in Virginia was Tsenacommacah.

50
00:02:25,207 --> 00:02:27,967
People had been saying those names for hundreds of years.

51
00:02:28,487 --> 00:02:32,007
Planting a flag was supposed to make the old names stop counting.

52
00:02:32,467 --> 00:02:33,407
But we still know them.

53
00:02:33,857 --> 00:02:34,954
And now you do too.
